Diagnostics (M6C, K31 investigation; off by default): a GPU trace for the Vulkan backend. With
--gpu_trace_frame=N (and --gpu_trace_frame_count=M) the draws of swaps N..N+M-1 are logged ([gputrace] lines:
shaders, render targets, texture fetch constants; for draws with a pixel shader also its depth, stencil, blend and
colour-control registers and the float constants it reads) with every resolve (copy registers, whether it went to the
scaled resolve buffer); with --gpu_trace_dir the data each resolve wrote (scaled when drawing at a resolution
scale) and the textures loaded from resolves are written there. While the trace is enabled the backend also logs
each distinct resolve and each pixel shader that reads the pixel position once, and dumps every cube texture it
loads. Each dump waits for the GPU. Used to find the first stage whose colours differ between scale 1 and 2, and
by the render-scale tests (tests/display) to compare the lighting cube maps.

